44:**Invariant 2: `htmlAttributes` never silently defaults.** `TryFrom<JsExtractOptions> for PipelineOptions` treats every `Option<T>` field as "use `PipelineOptions::default()`" when `None`, _except_ `html_attributes`, which goes through `HtmlAttributeMode::parse` and hard-errors, naming the bad value, if the caller (e.g. via a TypeScript `as any` cast bypassing the `'curated' | 'full' | 'none'` `ts_type`) passes something that isn't one of the three accepted strings. This is a deliberate application of AGENTS.md non-negotiable #6 ("never fail silently") at the boundary where TypeScript's type system stops being a real guarantee.
